      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/annevk/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/annevk/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2021-02-02T12:43:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-02-02T12:43:00Z",
    "body": "I think I prefer keeping policies as-is and not try to do something special for `document.open()`. While the URL changes the origin of the document does not. There was a time (and a browser) where `document.open()` was a lot more invasive but now it's only changing document state and none of that warrants policy inheritance in my book.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
